Web design pricing in Swansea — like most places — varies wildly. A cheap freelancer might quote £300. A large agency might quote £8,000 for the same brief. Neither figure tells you much about the value you'll actually get.

Here's a straightforward breakdown of what web design actually costs in Swansea and what you should expect at each level.

## What drives the cost of a Swansea website?

Before looking at price ranges, it helps to understand what you're actually paying for.

**Number of pages and complexity** — A five-page brochure site costs less than a twenty-page service site with a booking system, gallery, and blog. The more content and functionality required, the more it costs.

**Custom design vs templates** — Building from scratch costs more than adapting a purchased theme. But the result is a site that's unique to your business and built around your specific goals — not one that looks like fifty others.

**SEO foundations** — Some designers include on-page SEO as standard. Others don't. A website that can't be found on Google is not a good investment, regardless of how it looks.

**Who's doing the work** — An agency with account managers, project managers, and multiple departments has higher overheads than an independent studio. That cost gets passed to you.

**Ongoing costs** — Domain, hosting, maintenance, and support aren't always included in the upfront price. Make sure you understand the total cost, not just the day-one figure.

## Swansea web design price ranges

**From £199 — One-page WordPress starter site**

This is where NC Digital's entry-level builds sit. A focused one-page WordPress website gives you a professional online presence at a more accessible price point: not a throwaway template, but a purposefully built site using the right tools.

Well-suited to Swansea small businesses that need a solid, fast, SEO-ready website without the cost of a fully custom build.

**£800–£2,500 — Independent designer / small studio**

This is the range where you'll find independent Swansea web designers and small studios. A properly custom-designed website, on-page SEO foundations, and someone who understands your business before they start building. Most small business websites in Swansea sit here.

**£2,500–£6,000 — Complex projects**

Larger sites with [ecommerce](/services/ecommerce-development/), booking systems, custom integrations, or multiple service areas. The complexity justifies the cost — but make sure the additional features are things your business actually needs.

**£6,000+ — Agency territory**

At this level you're paying for agency overheads as much as the work. For most Swansea small businesses, this budget is better spent on a well-built site plus ongoing SEO investment.

## The monthly option — from £20/month inc. VAT

If a large upfront cost isn't practical, our [Managed Starter Website](/services/managed-starter-websites/) gives Swansea businesses a professionally built, fully managed website from £20/month inc. VAT — domain, hosting, and management included. Choose a tier with 5, 10, or unlimited new pages added monthly, with small changes included as standard.

One new customer from your website typically covers months of that cost.

## Don't optimise for the lowest price

The cheapest Swansea web designer is rarely the best value. A website that doesn't rank on Google, doesn't convert visitors into enquiries, or needs rebuilding in two years costs far more than one done properly the first time.

A website is a lead generation tool. The right question isn't "how cheap can I get this?" — it's "what's the cost of a website that actually works?"

